WEBVTT

01:32.120 --> 01:34.060
Now, then...

01:34.060 --> 01:37.100
Shall we bring this to its conclusion?

01:55.580 --> 01:58.800
One stepping past the wreckage of time...

02:01.390 --> 02:03.850
Who walks through the ashes...

02:06.270 --> 02:10.210
Lord of the wreckage of time...

02:11.140 --> 02:14.580
<i>It's nothing like when I read it in hiding.</i>

02:15.700 --> 02:19.480
<i>Perhaps it's made to be 
handled by human hands.</i>

02:35.190 --> 02:36.820
It reacted!

02:38.800 --> 02:39.970
Philomela?

02:40.540 --> 02:41.590
Philomela!

02:46.890 --> 02:51.340
You're a useless, dim-witted girl.

02:52.290 --> 02:54.910
If only you hadn't been born,

02:54.910 --> 03:01.080
Adam and Lilith might 
have managed to escape.

03:03.390 --> 03:04.370
Philomela!

03:05.010 --> 03:06.780
Philomela, are you all right?

03:06.780 --> 03:08.710
Something's interfering!

03:13.410 --> 03:19.720
If you'd been more capable, 
I wouldn't have had to hit you.

03:20.120 --> 03:22.530
But that's fine.

03:22.530 --> 03:27.140
I'm glad you were born incompetent.

03:27.460 --> 03:31.560
You're going to prove useful to 
me in the end, after all.

03:42.680 --> 03:46.390
You were the one who wanted me 
to be that way, Grandmother.

03:47.940 --> 03:50.510
All so that I would listen to you.

03:50.510 --> 03:54.530
So that I wouldn't be able 
to think about myself.

03:54.530 --> 03:55.330
You cursed me.

03:56.500 --> 03:59.430
But I was taught...

04:00.540 --> 04:01.760
I'm allowed to ignore you.

04:02.220 --> 04:03.050
To get angry.

04:03.670 --> 04:05.310
To shout.

04:05.710 --> 04:09.320
I can choose for myself 
and make my own wishes.

04:10.870 --> 04:13.810
So that's what I hope to do.

04:13.810 --> 04:15.140
That thing...

04:15.560 --> 04:18.700
Chise gave me this Thurisaz rune.

04:18.700 --> 04:23.240
The single letter of the rune 
has more than just one meaning.

04:28.580 --> 04:29.670
"Gate."

04:31.770 --> 04:32.450
"Giant."

04:34.210 --> 04:35.120
"Spirit."

04:37.540 --> 04:38.240
"Thorn."

04:40.260 --> 04:44.170
And... "Thor's hammer!"

04:46.290 --> 04:47.660
Philomela!

04:46.750 --> 04:52.290
Grandmother, I'm certain there's 
so much that I want to do.

04:52.700 --> 04:56.340
So I'm going to undo
 the curse you've put on me.

05:10.190 --> 05:11.300
Hey, are you...

05:11.300 --> 05:14.920
Everyone, hang on to me!

05:16.210 --> 05:17.240
Okay.

05:17.240 --> 05:18.960
You don't need to tell me.

05:19.840 --> 05:20.950
You can count on us.

05:26.320 --> 05:30.820
Here, a gate tantamount 
to an opening is closed.

05:31.400 --> 05:34.850
Rend from our world the withering fingers.

05:34.850 --> 05:37.260
Sever our gaze from the 
stars projected in the sky.

05:37.260 --> 05:42.220
Greet from unreachable distances 
the welcoming arms.

05:43.030 --> 05:45.220
She's taking my magic power!

05:49.260 --> 05:50.570
There's something there.

05:50.940 --> 05:52.170
Something else.

05:54.230 --> 05:58.600
So you've come, attracted by 
the scent to aid a heathen mother.

05:59.050 --> 06:02.300
My maiden is sought after by many indeed.

06:02.910 --> 06:07.040
I offer you a song of return to far away!

06:25.650 --> 06:26.850
Don't look.

06:54.230 --> 06:55.940
Are you up?

06:56.520 --> 06:58.370
Ow...

06:57.570 --> 06:59.600
What was I doing?

07:01.690 --> 07:03.320
Miss Veronica!

07:03.320 --> 07:05.190
Thank goodness.

07:10.700 --> 07:12.270
It's gone?

07:18.850 --> 07:21.170
That was a delightful song.

07:21.170 --> 07:24.260
Little maiden, shackled by a foreign god...

07:24.260 --> 07:26.500
You've freed yourself well.

07:26.500 --> 07:28.850
That concludes the festivities.

07:29.410 --> 07:32.410
I've not fought in such
 a fruitful battle in a long time.

07:32.960 --> 07:38.310
In recognition of this pleasure, I'll not 
demand any more compensation.

07:38.690 --> 07:44.310
My maiden, never forget the sacrifice.

07:48.790 --> 07:49.870
Yes.

08:09.380 --> 08:10.430
Hey there.

08:10.430 --> 08:12.090
That was rather pathetic.

08:12.090 --> 08:15.630
Your son doesn't exist anymore.

08:16.220 --> 08:17.860
I'm not Adam.

08:21.670 --> 08:26.150
Why didn't you come to kill me?

08:27.190 --> 08:29.280
You could have done it.

08:29.280 --> 08:31.840
You're my son, after all.

08:32.970 --> 08:35.260
You could have, too.

08:35.260 --> 08:36.940
Lizbeth Sargant.

08:38.040 --> 08:40.570
She was birthed by 
the woman you so despised.

08:40.570 --> 08:43.230
You could have killed her.

08:44.610 --> 08:46.660
But you didn't.

08:55.170 --> 08:58.930
I simply thought I could 
make use of her someday.

09:00.310 --> 09:02.180
What a pitiful woman.

09:03.310 --> 09:06.860
So strong that you couldn't 
welcome anyone inside.

09:06.860 --> 09:08.550
Nor did you try.

09:09.070 --> 09:12.190
In the end, nobody stayed by your side.

09:13.370 --> 09:15.540
My task appears to be complete, too.

09:19.640 --> 09:23.820
Goodbye, Adam's daughter.

09:36.130 --> 09:38.130
Grandmother, you...

09:38.130 --> 09:39.510
Spare me!

09:39.510 --> 09:43.350
I have no need for your words!

09:44.110 --> 09:45.940
There's something I want to ask.

09:46.290 --> 09:50.050
Why did you attack the Webster family?

09:51.430 --> 09:53.190
I need to know.

09:53.580 --> 09:57.660
I need to explain to Lucy.

09:59.770 --> 10:03.420
The fewer who know...

10:13.670 --> 10:15.340
You're pretty nimble!

10:15.680 --> 10:17.080
Zaccheroni!

10:18.940 --> 10:21.670
Hey, you're all alive.

10:22.200 --> 10:25.260
Turns out you're a pretty good babysitter.

10:25.260 --> 10:26.490
Same to you.

10:30.400 --> 10:31.980
I see.

10:31.980 --> 10:35.890
I don't know whose familiar that 
is, but that must be the target.

10:37.870 --> 10:38.690
Ruth!

10:38.690 --> 10:39.670
Right!

10:53.270 --> 10:54.050
Chise!

10:56.220 --> 10:57.260
My...

10:57.910 --> 10:59.570
My child...

11:00.080 --> 11:01.260
still lives!

11:06.130 --> 11:08.180
Chise, are you all right?

11:08.180 --> 11:09.130
Yes.

11:09.730 --> 11:11.120
The book...

11:12.120 --> 11:13.350
Philomela.

11:14.710 --> 11:17.010
Like what happens to Chise all the time.

11:17.010 --> 11:18.640
You've exhausted yourself.

11:18.640 --> 11:20.980
Elias, what do we do?

11:20.980 --> 11:22.140
The book...

11:22.140 --> 11:24.270
It's been stolen. There's nothing we can do.

11:24.790 --> 11:27.040
Looks like Zaccheroni is after it, anyway.

11:27.480 --> 11:30.000
You really don't care.

11:32.250 --> 11:33.210
Chise?

11:34.520 --> 11:40.510
Did I do well this time?

11:45.170 --> 11:47.840
Here we go again.

11:48.380 --> 11:49.650
Oh, you.

11:51.170 --> 11:52.340
Let's go home.

13:08.050 --> 13:09.190
You're up.

13:09.490 --> 13:10.560
Morning!

13:13.630 --> 13:15.360
Where were you?

13:15.930 --> 13:17.330
Where am I?

13:17.330 --> 13:19.560
I just came to get this.

13:20.290 --> 13:21.460
Mistletoe?

13:21.920 --> 13:22.950
Yeah.

13:22.950 --> 13:25.100
We're going to need it soon.

13:25.100 --> 13:26.810
We are?

13:26.810 --> 13:27.480
Um...

13:28.310 --> 13:30.710
This is Elias's and my place.

13:31.260 --> 13:35.240
We figured it'd be a pain to 
go back to the College, so...

13:35.970 --> 13:39.470
We're allowed to take some time off 
until the investigations start.

13:39.960 --> 13:43.790
Everyone else at College is on 
winter break, starting today.

13:44.380 --> 13:46.640
Winter break...

13:47.420 --> 13:49.620
I don't know what to think.

13:50.130 --> 13:53.120
What should I worry about first?

13:53.690 --> 13:58.480
Is there anything you want 
to do during the break?

13:59.700 --> 14:00.890
What about you?

14:04.850 --> 14:07.060
Decorating the tree.

14:07.060 --> 14:09.740
Year-end shopping, and...

14:11.390 --> 14:14.000
I want to try some 
party crackers this year.

14:15.140 --> 14:19.120
I gotta make some time for Silver, 
too, since we've been away.

14:22.480 --> 14:23.750
I...

14:26.540 --> 14:28.660
I want to make potpourri.

14:28.660 --> 14:29.790
With you.

14:34.850 --> 14:36.030
Of course!

14:37.050 --> 14:39.270
Wait! You're too fast!

14:39.500 --> 14:41.320
Have you tried running?

14:43.890 --> 14:44.640
Rían!

14:47.570 --> 14:48.920
Tory-san.

14:49.390 --> 14:50.480
Heya.

14:56.480 --> 14:57.580
You...

15:04.500 --> 15:05.800
I'm glad you're safe.

15:07.340 --> 15:09.600
The sun sleeps early.

15:09.600 --> 15:11.890
The moon and stars stay up all night.

15:12.580 --> 15:14.530
The night is coming.

15:14.530 --> 15:17.300
The long and short night is coming.

15:17.780 --> 15:19.070
Hello.

15:19.800 --> 15:23.240
Child of man, child of dragons, 
child of the goddess.

15:23.610 --> 15:28.310
The mother of winter is waiting 
eagerly at the hill to the east.

15:28.310 --> 15:30.590
You'd best be off.

15:31.090 --> 15:31.940
Yes.

15:35.780 --> 15:37.280
Tory.

15:37.280 --> 15:40.160
Could you take these two home?

15:40.460 --> 15:44.000
I'll go anywhere, 
as long as it's warm there.

15:48.000 --> 15:50.170
Philomela, are you all right?

15:51.480 --> 15:52.280
Yeah.

15:58.370 --> 15:59.960
Come on, let's go!

15:59.960 --> 16:01.640
I'm gonna freeze to death.

16:13.870 --> 16:15.060
You must be cold.

16:17.220 --> 16:18.080
Let's go.

16:21.010 --> 16:21.900
Okay.

16:27.550 --> 16:30.600
Where's that hill to the east?

16:31.100 --> 16:32.160
Chise.

16:32.160 --> 16:33.190
Over there.

17:22.060 --> 17:26.350
Thank you for giving Mother 
the snowdrop branches.

17:28.870 --> 17:33.560
May your next season be a bright one.

17:36.850 --> 17:41.950
You're really lucky she didn't ask for the 
heads of a hundred warriors or anything.

17:43.120 --> 17:46.850
You need to learn to say no.

17:46.850 --> 17:48.830
For real this time.

17:48.830 --> 17:49.980
Yes.

17:53.220 --> 17:54.220
Elias?

17:55.230 --> 17:56.490
These will be useful.

17:56.490 --> 17:58.410
And we can sell them, 
so let's take some home.

17:59.160 --> 18:00.970
The snowdrops?

18:00.970 --> 18:04.370
In some regions, it's said that if you 
find these before the end of the year,

18:04.370 --> 18:07.410
you'll be blessed with good luck.

18:07.410 --> 18:08.600
Huh...

18:10.740 --> 18:11.580
Here.

18:16.720 --> 18:18.930
It's such a pretty flower.

18:24.990 --> 18:26.410
So, for potpourri...

18:26.410 --> 18:28.820
The ingredients are really simple.

18:29.260 --> 18:31.300
We have plenty of needles, too.

18:31.300 --> 18:32.540
You can use whatever you want.

18:33.060 --> 18:35.230
Whatever I want?

18:35.230 --> 18:40.400
Oh, could I have some leftover 
fabric and needles and thread?

18:40.400 --> 18:43.070
I want to make some gifts for people, too.

18:43.070 --> 18:44.270
Of course.

19:36.610 --> 19:37.980
Well done.

19:38.360 --> 19:40.260
Did you acquire it?

19:40.870 --> 19:42.030
I see.

19:42.030 --> 19:43.350
Good for you.

19:45.730 --> 19:47.890
I brought a meal.

19:47.890 --> 19:50.120
How are you feeling?

19:53.260 --> 19:54.810
Thanks.

19:54.810 --> 19:56.110
I'll have it now.

20:01.710 --> 20:04.140
I can't eat anymore...

20:05.120 --> 20:07.920
Let's play cards next.

20:08.720 --> 20:11.080
We're having cream stew next, apparently.

20:11.080 --> 20:13.250
Insert happy shrieking noises.

20:13.250 --> 20:14.270
I'm still good for more.

20:14.270 --> 20:15.830
Seriously?

20:15.830 --> 20:17.730
Huh? Where's Chise?

20:21.840 --> 20:23.480
Silver made some.

20:24.210 --> 20:26.820
I told you, I don't need any.

20:45.410 --> 20:46.550
So...

20:47.210 --> 20:49.880
What did you have to sacrifice 
in order to survive this time?

20:50.880 --> 20:53.730
I think I did what I could.

20:54.250 --> 21:01.430
But because of that, a lot of people 
died, and I didn't do anything about it.

21:02.490 --> 21:03.740
And?

21:04.380 --> 21:07.420
I told myself it had to be done.

21:16.220 --> 21:18.270
I told you.

21:18.270 --> 21:21.000
What's the difference between you and me?

21:21.000 --> 21:24.200
You've finally learned 
to put yourself first.

21:24.200 --> 21:25.530
Congrats.

21:26.870 --> 21:29.510
It's not like I wanted that.

21:29.510 --> 21:31.750
That's still the result.

21:34.640 --> 21:35.990
C'mon.

21:42.620 --> 21:44.770
Something I let go of.

21:45.650 --> 21:47.900
Something I wanted and got.

21:48.960 --> 21:50.780
Something I want to cherish.

21:52.130 --> 21:53.650
Something I cut loose.

21:55.970 --> 22:02.570
I still don't know what's right, 
and I still need to go on?

22:09.610 --> 22:11.340
You still haven't decided?

22:14.570 --> 22:18.670
I don't know what my preferences are.

22:23.780 --> 22:25.530
Uh... um...

22:25.780 --> 22:28.250
You don't need to choose just one.

22:30.480 --> 22:32.020
There's plenty.

22:32.720 --> 22:35.390
Plenty of time, too.

22:36.070 --> 22:38.520
Hey, show me that card.

22:38.520 --> 22:39.680
Not happening.

22:39.680 --> 22:41.060
Don't push me!

22:57.880 --> 22:59.920
What are you doing?!

22:59.920 --> 23:01.300
Um....

23:01.300 --> 23:02.430
What's this about?

23:02.430 --> 23:03.650
Sorry!

23:46.010 --> 23:50.930
I can't be your ally this time around.
